---
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
import logo from '../../public/favicon/web-app-manifest-512x512.png';
import homepageSchema from "../assets/homepage-schema.svg"
const resourceLinks = [
    {
        label: 'Documentation',
        href: 'https://docs.medatarun.com',
        description: 'Install, learn the concepts, and follow the quickstart.'
    },
    {
        label: 'Source code',
        href: 'https://github.com/medatarun/medatarun',
        description: 'Dive into the repository, contribute, or reuse building blocks.'
    },
    {
        label: 'Discord',
        href: 'https://discord.gg/626262',
        description: 'Discuss data models, use cases, and design decisions.'
    }
];

const adoptionScenarios = [
    'Teams disagree on definitions.',
    'Governance is scattered across static documents.',
    'AI starts consuming data and “guessing” becomes a risk.'
];
---

<section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero__content">
        <div style={{display: "grid", gridTemplateColumns: "5em 1fr", gap: "2rem"}}>
            <div>
                <Image src={logo} alt="Medatarun logo" style={{width: "100%", height: "auto", borderRadius: "1em"}}/>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h1>Medatarun</h1>
                <h2>An open source system to define and share explicit data models across teams and tools.</h2>
                <p class="lede">Making data meaning explicit, so teams and AI can rely on it.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align:center; margin-top:2rem; margin-left:auto; margin-right: auto; width: 40em; max-width: 100%;">
            <Image src={homepageSchema} alt="Schema diagram of Medatarun"
                   style={{backgroundColor: "transparent", width: "100%", height: "auto"}}/>
        </div>
        <div class="hero__actions">
            <a class="button button--primary" href="https://docs.medatarun.com/docs/intro">Documentation &
                Quickstart</a>
            <a class="button button--ghost" href="https://github.com/medatarun/medatarun">Explore GitHub</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<main class="page">
    <section class="section" id="real-issue">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section__header">
                <h2>Why Medatarun</h2>
            </div>
            <div>

                <p>Most data stacks focus on storage, processing, and delivery.
                    Governance focuses on rules, ownership, and processes.
                    Documentation lives in tools that are rarely shared or enforced.</p>

                <p>What is missing is a single place where data meaning itself is defined,
                    explicitly, structurally, and in a way that both humans and machines can use.</p>

                <p>This gap shows up differently depending on who you are:</p>

                <div class="">
                    <ul>
                        <li>For CIOs, CTOs, and data leaders, it creates fragile systems and constant alignment work.
                        </li>
                        <li>For business teams, it leads to unclear definitions, conflicting indicators, low trust,
                            communication is hard with IT.
                        </li>
                        <li>For AI initiatives, it results in systems that guess instead of reasoning.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <p>The problem is not data, tools, or infrastructure.
                    It is the absence of a shared, explicit and living reference for data meaning.</p>

                <p>Static documentation has no operational value. That’s why it fails.</p>

                <p>Medatarun makes data models operable.</p>

                <p><i>If you want the full reasoning, <a
                        href="https://docs.medatarun.com/docs/resources/problem_en">you can read the complete problem
                    statement.</a></i></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section muted" id="what-medatarun-does">

        <div class="container">
            <div class="section__header">
                <h2>What Medatarun is</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="split">
                <div>
                    <p>
                        Medatarun is an open source software that manages data models as explicit,
                        shared artifacts instead of leaving them implicit in code, or spread across
                        dashboards, Excel, Word files or wikis.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        These models describe entities, relationships, attributes, rules, and operations
                        that define the meaning of data.
                    </p>
                    <p>Everything can be tagged and fully documented.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="pill-list">
                    <p>Medatarun exposes these models through:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>A user interface to explore, enrich and discuss them</li>
                        <li>APIs and CLI tools for developers and tools</li>
                        <li>Structured access (MCP) for AI agents</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <p>Medatarun does not store business data and does not replace your data stack.</p>
                    <p>
                        It provides a concrete software layer where data meaning is defined,
                        enriched, queried, and shared by humans and tools.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p>
                    Medatarun is built with a plugin system.
                    With plugins, you and your teams can add domain-specific commands, import or sync models from live
                    systems,
                    and connect and relate models to databases, alerting systems, and automated workflows.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

    </section>


    <section class="section" id="why-now">
        <div class="container split">
            <div>
                <h2>When Medatarun becomes useful</h2>
            </div>
            <div>
                <p>It becomes relevant:</p>
                <ul class="list">
                    <li>when teams disagree on data definitions,</li>
                    <li>when governance is done in scattered documents,</li>
                    <li>when AI starts consuming data and “guessing” becomes a risk.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>In these situations, making data meaning explicit becomes a prerequisite.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="using">
        <div class="container split">
            <div>
                <h2>Working with Medatarun</h2>
                <p>Use it when structure and meaning become the bottleneck.</p>
                <p>
                    Medatarun is open source and early-stage.
                    It is not a turnkey product, but a tool used during
                    your analytics, development, governance and AI projects.
                </p>
                <p>
                    I’m an independent interim CTO/CIO (seij).
                    In missions, Medatarun is one of the tools I use when a shared,
                    explicit data model is the missing piece.
                </p>
                <p>
                    This work typically happens upstream:
                    to align business and IT, reduce ambiguity, and de-risk data or AI initiatives.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If you want to discuss your context:
                    <a href="https://www.seij.net">https://www.seij.net</a>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="section" id="explore">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section__header">
                <p class="section__eyebrow">Explore Medatarun</p>
                <h2>Start learning, building, and discussing.</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="card-grid resources">
                {resourceLinks.map((resource) => (
                        <a class="card resource-card" href={resource.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                            <div class="resource-card__label">{resource.label}</div>
                            <p>{resource.description}</p>
                            <span class="resource-card__link">Visit {resource.label}</span>
                        </a>
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

</main>

<style>
    :global(body) {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: 'Inter', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial,
        sans-serif;
        background: #0c0d11;
        color: #0f1b36;
    }

    :global(main) {
        margin: 0;
    }

    :global(#root) {
        min-height: 100vh;
    }

    :root {
        --hero-bg: radial-gradient(circle at 0% 0%, #101727, #05070d 60%);
        --hero-panel: rgba(7, 10, 20, 0.8);
        --primary: #3578e5;
        --surface: #ffffff;
        --muted-surface: #f7f8fb;
        --border: #e3e7f2;
        --text: #0f1b36;
        --text-muted: #5a6070;
        --radius: 16px;
        --shadow: 0 25px 70px rgba(5, 8, 20, 0.35);
        --shadow-soft: 0 10px 40px rgba(15, 27, 54, 0.1);
    }

    a {
        color: var(--primary);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    a:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .hero {
        background: var(--hero-bg);
        color: #edf1ff;
        padding: 5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    .hero::after {
        content: '';
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(53, 120, 229, 0.25), transparent 60%);
        filter: blur(50px);
    }

    .hero__content {
        position: relative;
        z-index: 1;
        max-width: 960px;
    }

    .hero__statements {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .hero__statements p {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
        background: var(--hero-panel);
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.5;
        color: rgba(237, 241, 255, 0.85);
    }

    .hero__actions {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        margin-top: 2rem;
        justify-content: center;
    }

    .button {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.85rem 1.8rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        border: 1px solid transparent;
        transition: transform 200ms ease, box-shadow 200ms ease, border-color 200ms ease;
    }

    .button:hover {
        transform: translateY(-1px);
        text-decoration: none;
    }

    .button--primary {
        background: var(--primary);
        color: #fff;
        box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(53, 120, 229, 0.3);
    }

    .button--ghost {
        background: transparent;
        color: #edf1ff;
        border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
    }

    .eyebrow {
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.2em;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        color: rgba(237, 241, 255, 0.75);
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .lede {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: rgba(237, 241, 255, 0.85);
    }

    .page {
        background: #f5f6fb;
        color: var(--text);
    }

    .container {
        max-width: 1100px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 1.5rem;
    }

    .section {
        padding: 4rem 0;
        background: var(--surface);
    }

    .section.muted {
        background: var(--muted-surface);
    }

    .section + .section {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .section__eyebrow {
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .section__header {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    h1,
    h2,
    h3 {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
    }

    h1 {
        font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    }

    p {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .split {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
        gap: 2.5rem;
        align-items: start;
    }

    .card-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
        gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .card {
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    }

    .card h3 {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .section__footer {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    .pill-list {
        background: #fff;
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
    }

    .pill-list ul {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .pill-list li {
        background: #eff3ff;
        border-radius: 999px;
        padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .list {
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
        margin: 0;
    }

    .resources .card {
        background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffffff 0%, #f7f8fb 100%);
    }

    .resource-card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.5rem;
    }

    .resource-card__label {
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .resource-card__link {
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--primary);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
        .hero {
            padding-top: 4rem;
        }

        .hero__actions {
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: stretch;
        }

        .section {
            padding: 3rem 0;
        }
    }
</style>
